# Example only. Do not fill in this file: it is tracked by git, and a key typed here ships with the next commit.
# The real one is ~/.config/kite-mcp-server/env, outside any repo and readable only by you
# (tools/setup-trader.sh writes it). Type your Kite Connect key and secret there, never in the chat.
#
# For a self-hosted zerodha/kite-mcp-server (github.com/zerodha/kite-mcp-server): the hosted
# mcp.kite.trade leaves out the order tools. Run ONE shared copy in HTTP mode (APP_MODE=http,
# APP_HOST=127.0.0.1, APP_PORT=8080; never stdio, which cannot log in) and connect Claude Code to
# http://127.0.0.1:8080/mcp. Your Kite Connect app's Redirect URL: http://127.0.0.1:8080/callback.
# Orders only work from the static IP you registered in Kite (SEBI rule since 1 Apr 2026).
# The order tools are Needs approval in Claude, never Always allow.
# Delete the EXCLUDED_TOOLS line only when you go live.
KITE_API_KEY=IN_THE_KEY_FILE_NOT_HERE_NEVER_IN_CHAT
KITE_API_SECRET=IN_THE_KEY_FILE_NOT_HERE_NEVER_IN_CHAT
EXCLUDED_TOOLS=place_order,modify_order,cancel_order,place_gtt_order,modify_gtt_order,delete_gtt_order
